    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The synthesized intelligence assessment reveals a globally elevated US military posture, with concentrated operational activity in the Indo-Pacific and European theaters. In the Pacific, the USS Theodore Roosevelt (CVN-71) strike group has concluded RIMPAC 2026 exercises and is transiting to the Western Pacific, while the USS George Washington (CVN-73) strike group remains deployed in Da Nang, Vietnam—the first carrier visit since 2023—accompanied by USS Robert Smalls (CG-62) and USS Shoup (DDG-86). This reinforces US strategic engagement in Southeast Asia amid regional tensions. Submarine operations are robust, with USS Minnesota (SSN-783) completing its inaugural forward-deployment to Guam, enhancing rotational presence in the Indo-Pacific. In Europe, USAF platforms demonstrate high operational tempo, with C-17, C-30J, and A400M aircraft supporting NATO logistics, training, and humanitarian missions across the continent. High-speed tankers (K35R) and AWACS (E-3TF) aircraft in the Mediterranean and central US underscore sustained airborne early warning and aerial refueling capabilities. Notably, the 52.4% reduction in Strait of Hormuz transits since the Iran-US conflict began suggests deliberate de-escalation, though Houthi threats to Saudi tankers in Yemen persist. Fleet modernization is evident with the inactivation of USS Georgia (SSGN-729) and USS Fort Worth (LCS-3), temporarily reducing operational capacity. Overall, the data indicates a US military prioritizing global readiness, with particular emphasis on countering regional adversaries and reinforcing allied operations in the Indo-Pacific and Europe. The strategic environment remains dynamic, with concurrent exercises, port visits, and submarine deployments reflecting a deliberate effort to maintain deterrence and operational flexibility.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
